  "caveats": [
    "Compaction is represented only by a porosity decrease with unchanged retention parameters.",
    "Crust destruction and surface disturbance (which may matter more) are not modelled.",
    "The response is not monotone: in the dry baseline a little compaction raises activation (the same water fills less pore space, so the soil is wetter) while diffusion falls; uptake peaks near porosity 0.36 and falls beyond (checked by direct porosity scan). Biochar (higher porosity) moves the other way.",
    "Rub' al Khali soil and community; not a prediction for other soils"
